Adopted plainly: gen_pfa_large r5's map_step_pair, gen_layout r5's gl_map8 exit-fusion shape, gen_batchlane r5's div-vs-rcp locality lesson. Two findings worth noting: the fused exit **loses** at L=100 (+8–10%, 3/3 — gated to L≤80), and growing `pln_s8_step` silently un-inlined `pln_foldw` (gcc dropped its constprop clones), costing @s3 at L=31 ~5–9% until I made the map specialization explicit — caught by the symbol-table audit, recorded as a lesson for the panel. Full sweep L=2..128 passes, round-6 drill (45/48/54/63/96/104/127 at B=8) all plan and pass within budget, AVX2 fallback verified, wisdom keys stripped at round end, and only `impl/gen_planner.c` + `strategies/gen_planner.md` were written.
